      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1041663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-28T18:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a routing table in the NFC chip which keeps track of how/where data should be routed.\nSystem code matching is one of the method. Every technique needs to have a default, where all the packets are routed to some environment if there wasn\u0027t any matching. This would provide an option for the vendor to define what the default behavior should be.\n\nSystem Code routing is defined in NCI Specification.",
      "parentUuid": "02fc5ac5_b584cee2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 33
